{
  "decision": "map_front",
  "rationale": "The iterative family dominates the front with luts_plus_ffs=257, far below the 1500 HV reference, while pipelined/pipelined_m are 3-5x larger. The front currently covers only a narrow slice of the accuracy range (10.3-12.2 bits) and area range (257-295). To maximize hypervolume, we must map the full trade-off curve for the iterative family, specifically exploring the trade-off between n_iter (accuracy) and data_width/angle_guard (area) to see if we can push accuracy higher without excessive area cost, or if we can reduce area further at the cost of accuracy. Since all families are explored and iterative is the clear winner, a code-driven NSGA-II search over the full iterative parameter space is the most efficient way to complete the front mapping within the remaining budget.",
